<script>
  import reports from '#lib/data/reports-4471.json';
  import notes from '#lib/data/desk-notes.json';
  import { groupByCause, readAs, uniqueById } from '#lib/kb/causes';
  import { tenantOf } from '#lib/kb/locales';
  import SplitTable from '#lib/kb/SplitTable.svelte';
  import Callout from '#lib/kb/Callout.svelte';
  import RenderStamp from '#lib/kb/RenderStamp.svelte';

  const rows = reports.filter((r) => r.mergedInto === 4471).length;
  const merged = uniqueById(reports).filter((r) => r.mergedInto === 4471);
  const groups = groupByCause(merged, tenantOf);
  const count = (cause) => groups.find((g) => g.cause === cause)?.reports.length ?? 0;
  const shifted = groups.reduce((n, g) => n + readAs(g, notes.oneDayMove), 0);
  const mistagged = groups.flatMap((g) => g.reports.filter((r) => r.meta.intakeTag !== g.cause)).length;
  const tickets = {
    parser: 'https://github.com/Rhinomcd/support-kb/issues/1',
    hint: 'https://github.com/Rhinomcd/support-kb/issues/2',
    shift: 'https://github.com/Rhinomcd/support-kb/issues/3',
  };
</script>

[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) holds **{merged.length} reports** as one bug: the parser reads
dates month first. That bug is real and covers most of them. It is not the only one in there.

<Callout kind="warn">
#4471 is three problems with three different fixes. The parser fix alone leaves
{count('hint') + shifted} of these reports broken.
</Callout>

## The split

<SplitTable ticket={4471} {tickets} />

Counts are the desk's own cause view, the one the #4471 page runs: each report is counted under
the cause its tenant and channel give it. The one-day moves stay counted where the desk files
them, under `parser`, and get their own ticket.

The export has {rows} rows for #4471. Its pages overlap, so some reports appear twice; the
table counts each report id once.

## How to tell them apart

Read the dates in the report, then look up the tenant (`src/lib/data/tenants/`). Every tenant on
file writes the day first.

- **Day and month swapped, any channel except a booking-v3 form:** [parser]({tickets.parser}).
  7 April comes out as 4 July. Reports through booking-v2 forms land here too: v2's hint says
  `DD/MM/YYYY`, so people type day first and the parser flips it.
- **Day and month swapped, through a booking-v3 form:** [hint]({tickets.hint}). The form prints
  `MM/DD/YYYY` under the field, people type what it says, and the form reads it day first. Only
  `alder.physio`, `copper.studio` and `pale.harbour` run booking-v3.
- **The date moved by one day:** [shift]({tickets.shift}). 12 May shown as 11 May, Tuesday shown
  as Monday, an invite that arrived before the booking. No swap produces that. The desk already
  listed these in `desk-notes.json`; the #4471 table files them under `parser` and footnotes them.

Do not go by the intake tag. Intake guesses it from the reporter's browser before anyone reads
the report, and it names the wrong problem on {mistagged} of these.

## Why one ticket held three

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject line. All three problems
arrive as "Wrong day on the invite" or "Month and day swapped?", so subject matching put them in
one thread, and the queue then read as one bug. The subject says how the reporter felt; the dates
in the body and the tenant say which bug it is.

## What changes

- Fix the parser and the booking-v3 hint separately. Ship the hint fix with the parser fix, or
  booking-v3 tenants stay wrong.
- Investigate the one-day shift as its own bug: it looks like a time-zone conversion, not
  parsing.
- When a date report comes in, match it to a ticket by its problem, not its subject. 0001 needs a
  new decision record to replace it.

<RenderStamp {signature} />
